From 6f4323580c6946286e8806ec7782ac79f8eb1dd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 18:17:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] kaiair: UL closed-loop power control, apply TPC at the
 nrUE PHY (fix #830)

Stock OAI nrUE decodes the DCI TPC but never applies it (open-loop PUSCH),
so the gNB UL power-control loop never closes. Implement the UE side behind
KAIAIR_UL_PWR_APPLY (default off = bit-for-bit stock):

- nr_ue_scheduler.c: stop zeroing the decoded delta_pusch (gated) so it flows
  into the f_b_f_c accumulator; pass &pcmax to expose P_CMAX.
- nr_ue_power_procedures.c + mac_proto.h: get_pusch_tx_power_ue() returns P_CMAX
  via a new out-param.
- fapi_nr_ue_interface.h: carry pcmax_dBm on the PUSCH PDU (rides the MAC->PHY copy).
- nr_ulsch_ue.c: scale PUSCH symbol amplitude (data + DMRS + PT-RS) from the
  absolute tx_power via 10^((tx_power-P_CMAX)/20) (Option B; AMP == P_CMAX full
  scale), with a -20 dB safety floor. apply=0 keeps the legacy path identical.

HW-verified on ARA (X310 gNB + B210 UE): gNB drives the UE from max down to a
regulated operating point via standard 3GPP TPC; UL SINR tracks the Cantelli
target. Both raise and lower directions confirmed.
